    "datePosted": "2026-10-29T07:16:34.000000Z",
    "description": "HEAD OF PROGRAMS — ETHIOPIA Job Title: Head of Programs — Ethiopia Organization: ForAfrika Duty Station: Addis Ababa, Ethiopia (with regular travel to field locations up to 40%) Division: Ethiopia Country Office Job Level: Mid-Senior / Management Contract Type: Contract Post Date: October 28, 2026 Application Deadline: November 11, 2026 ABOUT FORAFRIKA ForAfrika is an African-rooted, globally connected organisation dedicated to empowering communities across the continent through sustainable development and humanitarian aid. With over 40 years of operational experience, ForAfrika works in environments that vary from emergency relief settings to long-term development, ensuring that every initiative is contextually aligned with the needs of the people it serves. Through a deep love for Africa and unwavering commitment, ForAfrika delivers programmes that transform lives by embracing an integrated approach to development. This includes enhancing education, health and nutrition, water and sanitation, food security and livelihoods, economic empowerment, and more, building environments where all Africans can thrive. POSITION SUMMARY The Head of Programs is responsible for leading all programmatic functions across the organization's operations, ensuring high-quality, accountable, and sustainable programming that aligns with strategic objectives and responds to community needs. This senior leadership role encompasses oversight of program implementation, quality assurance, community integration, Design, Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability, and Learning (DMEAL), and emergency response coordination. The successful candidate will provide visionary leadership to drive program excellence while building organizational capacity and fostering partnerships that amplify impact. REPORTING RELATIONSHIPS Solid-Line Reporting: Country Director Dotted-Line Reporting: Director of Programs, Global Support Office (provides technical oversight, guidance, and capacity building on programmatic matters) KEY ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES Strategic Program Leadership & Quality Assurance Provide strategic direction and oversight for all programmatic activities across multiple sectors including health, education, WASH, food security, livelihoods, and emergencyresponse. Establish and maintain program quality frameworks ensuring adherence to international standards including SPHERE, Core Humanitarian Standard (CHS), and donor compliance requirements. Lead the development and implementation of the country program strategy in alignment with organizational mission and donor requirements. Ensure all programs are designed and implemented in ways responsive to community needs, cultural contexts, and beneficiary feedback. Champion innovation in program design and implementation methodologies to enhance effectiveness and sustainability. Program Implementation Management Oversee portfolio of programs with collective budgets and ensure efficient resource allocation across initiatives. Monitor program performance against targets, timelines, and budgetary allocations, implementing corrective measures as needed. Lead program proposal development processes, ensuring technical quality, contextual relevance, and competitive positioning. Coordinate with finance team on budget variance analysis (BVA) and financial reporting to ensure fiscal accountability. Establish and maintain relationships with key donors, government partners, and implementing partners. Community Integration & Partnership Development Ensure meaningful community participation in all phases of the program cycle from design through evaluation. Establish and maintain strategic partnerships with local organizations, government entities, and community leaders. Lead the development of community engagement strategies that promote local ownership and sustainability. Oversee capacity-building initiatives for community-based organizations and local partners. Ensure cultural sensitivity and conflict-sensitive programming approaches across all interventions. Emergency Response & Humanitarian Coordination Lead organizational preparedness for emergency response including development and regular updating of contingency plans. Coordinate rapid response to humanitarian crises, ensuring timely and effective assistance delivery. Represent the organization in humanitarian coordination forums and cluster meetings. Maintain emergency supply stocks and ensure readiness of response teams and equipment. Lead needs assessments and response strategy development during humanitarian emergencies. Team Leadership & Organizational Development Provide leadership and mentorship to program managers, MEAL officers, field coordinators, and technical specialists. Build organizational capacity through staff development planning, training coordination, and performance management. Foster a collaborative work environment that promotes professional growth and high performance. Establish clear performance expectations and accountability mechanisms for all program staff. Champion organizational values and ensure adherence tothe code of conduct and safeguarding policies. External Relations & Representation Serve as primary liaison with donors, government officials, and partner organizations on programmatic matters. Represent the organization at national and international forums, conferences, and coordination meetings. Develop and maintain strategic relationships that enhance program effectiveness and organizational profile. Lead resource mobilization efforts and contribute to fundraising strategy development. Ensure compliance with government regulations and maintain positive relationships with authorities.",
